# SYNOPSIS

```usage
vx command [argument ...]
```

# DESCRIPTION

`vx` is the one command a developer runs on the dev machine.
SwiftPM builds it; it starts CMake, Ninja, QEMU and the other tools, and builds, tests, boots and checks the tree with them.
Run it from the repository's root, after building it first, so that the builds it starts don't wait on SwiftPM's lock:

```rc
% swift build --product vx && .build/debug/vx ci
```

Its commands are:

| Command | Does | Page |
| `build [arch ...]` | configure and build each arch's tree | vx-build(1) |
| `test [arch ...]` | build, then run each arch's QEMU tests, or only what a change risks | vx-build(1) |
| `boot [arch]` | build and boot interactively | vx-build(1) |
| `bench` | the boot budgets, judged against this machine's history | vx-bench(1) |
| `trace` | collect, print and summarise traces | vx-trace(1) |
| `loc` | lines per component, and the size budgets | vx-loc(1) |
| `man` | read and check the manual | vx-man(1) |
| `hardware` | the hardware support list | vx-hardware(1) |
| `rc-oracle` | our rc against 9front's | vx-rc-oracle(1) |
| `acpi` | the corpus of firmware tables | vx-acpi(1) |
| `ci` | everything above that checks, in order | vx-ci(1) |
| `elf2efi`, `mkbootfs`, `check-pixels`, `qemu-monitor`, `mathgen` | build steps | vx-steps(1) |

An <arch> is `amd64`, `arm64` or `rv64`.
Any other word is refused with the three names.
The build steps and `trace` run from any directory; every other command refuses to run unless the current directory holds `Package.swift` and `CMakePresets.json`.

A step that `vx` runs for you writes its output to `build/vx/<step>.log` and shows only the last 30 lines if it fails.
After each step `vx` prints a line such as `vx: amd64-build ok (41 s)`.
Every command exits 0 on success and 1 on failure.

# FILES

: `build/<arch>/`
  The CMake tree of each arch.
: `build/vx/<step>.log`
  The output of each step.

# SEE ALSO

vx-build(1), vx-ci(1), vx-steps(1), vx-man(1)

# DIAGNOSTICS

`vx: unknown command <name>; ...` for a word it doesn't know, and `vx: run vx <command> from the repository root` outside the root.
